<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahajirstvo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1860s–1870s</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Muhajir exodus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mahajirstvo is the name given to the mass emigration and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportation</a> of Muslim peoples of the north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, including the Abkhaz and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circassians">Circassians</a>, to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> after the Russian conquest. In Abkhazia it followed the abolition of the principality in 1864 and the revolts of 1866 and 1877, and it greatly reduced the Abkhaz population, leaving large districts empty.</p></div>
